Now I'll implement paasio.go. The consistency test requires that ReadCount returns nops == n/numBytes. Each Read returns len(p) bytes (50). Since the counters are updated atomically per operation (both bytes and op count are updated within the same critical section), nops will always equal n/50.

Note: nops is `int`, and the test computes `expectedOps := n / numBytes` (int64) and compares with `int64(nops)`. No problem.

Implementation:

```go
package paasio

import (
	"io"
	"sync"
)

type readCounter struct {
	mu   sync.Mutex
	r    io.Reader
	n    int64
	nops int
}

func NewReadCounter(r io.Reader) ReadCounter {
	return &readCounter{r: r}
}

func (rc *readCounter) Read(p []byte) (int, error) {
	n, err := rc.r.Read(p)
	rc.mu.Lock()
	rc.n += int64(n)
	rc.nops++
	rc.mu.Unlock()
	return n, err
}

func (rc *readCounter) ReadCount() (int64, int) {
	rc.mu.Lock()
	defer rc.mu.Unlock()
	return rc.n, rc.nops
}
```

